__pycache__/
*.pyc
hybrid_small/*.bin
hybrid_small/ks_*/

# Benchmark datasets: the .bin files are 2.8 GB each and the ks_* directories
# are regenerable Kilosort output. The small files beside them -- truth.npz,
# manifest.csv, probe.json -- ARE tracked, because they are what makes a result
# reproducible and they are only kilobytes.
hybrid_tiered/*.bin
hybrid_tiered/ks_*/
hybrid_v2_rep*/*.bin
hybrid_v2_rep*/ks_*/

# Heavy analysis products under outputs/. GitHub hard-rejects any file over
# 100 MB, so a single one of these makes a push impossible rather than merely
# slow -- and the failure is silent, a push that hangs instead of erroring.
# These are all regenerable from the scripts plus the raw recording; the small
# CSV/JSON/PNG summaries beside them stay tracked.
#
# This list exists because `git add -A` run from a SUBDIRECTORY stages the
# whole repository, not that directory. One such call swept a 2.6 GB .bin and
# ~2 GB of parquet/pkl into a commit, and the resulting push could never
# succeed.
outputs/*.parquet
outputs/*.pkl
outputs/*.npy
outputs/*.npz
outputs/bombcell_results*/
outputs/*_cache_*.pkl
outputs/verdicts/
*.dat
*.bin
